{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Acute angle <math alttext=\"upper P\"><mi>P</mi>\n</math> has a measure of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> radians, and acute angle <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> has a measure of <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> radians. The function <math alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi>\n</math> is defined by <math alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals p left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis Superscript x Baseline plus 6 t\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi></math>. If <math alttext=\"sine p equals cosine t\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>t</mi></math>, which of the following represents the value <math alttext=\"g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> in terms of <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math>?</p>", "keys": ["ce3307c1-1464-45f8-9fe4-95a5f566edb2"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "8606f0d6-680a-4634-8d9f-a745353b78f8", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"6 t plus pi\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t<mi>t</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mi>&pi;</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "fade4dc3-4fce-4852-b454-e3531948af29", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"6 t\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t<mi>t</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "312984fa-508f-4c6e-be26-0539e72ec40c", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"5 t plus pi\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t\t<mi>t</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mi>&pi;</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "ce3307c1-1464-45f8-9fe4-95a5f566edb2", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"5 t plus StartFraction pi Over 2 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t\t<mi>t</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<mi>&pi;</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It&rsquo;s given that acute angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper P\"><mi>P</mi></math> has a measure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi></math> radians and that acute angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi></math> has a measure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> radians. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"sine p equals cosine t\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>t</mi></math>, it follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p plus t equals StartFraction normal pi Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p equals StartFraction normal pi Over 2 EndFraction minus t\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></math>. It&rsquo;s also given that function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi></math> is defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals p left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis Superscript x Baseline plus 6 t\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi></math>. To determine the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> in terms of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math>, substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction normal pi Over 2 EndFraction minus t\"><mfrac><mo>&#960;</mo><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals p left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis Superscript x Baseline plus 6 t\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals left parenthesis StartFraction normal pi Over 2 EndFraction minus t right parenthesis left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis Superscript 0 Baseline plus 6 t\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mo>&#960;</mo><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals left parenthesis StartFraction normal pi Over 2 EndFraction minus t right parenthesis left parenthesis 1 right parenthesis plus 6 t\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mo>&#960;</mo><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi></math>. This is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals StartFraction normal pi Over 2 EndFraction minus t plus 6 t\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals 5 t plus StartFraction normal pi Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 t plus StartFraction pi Over 2 EndFraction\"><mn>5</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> represents the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> in terms of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>", "externalid": "1ef8e9cb-4e5c-441a-9395-222ae1a20a61", "correct_answer": ["D"]}